  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the metaphorical 'solution' scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the 'after' scene (the crater) which represents the violent annihilation of the Middle East as the 'solution' to terrorism. This projection is implicit, as the meme uses the user's perspective to imagine themselves as the one who has 'solved' the problem by destroying the region, thereby internalizing the meme's violent and reductive message. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the framing of 'before' and 'after' creates a participatory illusion where the viewer is positioned as the agent of the 'solution'.",
